{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/374797-first-time-setting-help","id":374797,"title":"First Time, Setting Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-18T20:36:52-08:00","id":374797,"title":"First Time, Setting Help","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I would like to ask for some guidance, I'm going to be running my first nWoD game (Hunter) &amp; I would like to set it up in a made up Ohioan town. I want it to be about the size a large town, without being an urban center like the capitol Columbus. I would like guidance on how many supernatural things should be in the town &amp; how frequently I should have the Hunters fight/kill them. I'm unsure how to make each session engaging if the monster always gets away. Even if it is supposed to be a long antagonist arc. The Hunters need to hunt things but if they hunt too well then they will depopulate the town &amp; they'll have to move. I'd almost like to introduce a Buffy-like excuse to have more than normal supernaturals, like a Verge or something. The only thought I had was that the town is supernaturally important &amp; the Hunters first real long arc villians would be monsters who have staked out the territory, when the hunters kill them there is a power vacuum &amp; it all escalates with more &amp; varying monsters coming from near &amp; far.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Any advice or comments?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T13:57:18-08:00","id":375566,"title":"","content":"Speaking as someone who lives in a rural area, a small town usually also &quot;includes&quot; people living in the surrounding area. The hamlet I live in has maybe a couple hundred people in the actual &quot;town&quot; area, even though the actual township includes a couple thousand people.<br /> <br /> There's a <i>lot</i> of room right there; heck, you can have them &quot;cover&quot; nearby towns as well, if you feel that just one is constraining.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest against using monsters that require a lot of infrastructure; something like vampires, who would stick out like a sore thumb. Instead, go for monsters that work in groups, or that make their own infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Maybe a werewolf pack has decided that the place is their pack's territory; maybe a cult has moved in because it's relatively &quot;off the grid&quot;. Maybe the graveyard by the church actually <i>is</i> haunted. And the thing is? You don't need monsters, exactly - see if you can find a copy of Mysterious Places anywhere, and read the chapter about The Statue of Weeping Alice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T14:04:40-08:00","id":375572,"title":"","content":"You could just have there be a few months between each hunt, unless some serious supernatural thing is going on. Like; &quot;Ok, you killed the murderous Vampire. You go back to your jobs on Monday, and nothing of interest happens for like 6 months. THEN, rumor start to circulate of wierd chantings comming from the woods at night&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T15:01:16-08:00","id":377557,"title":"","content":"I want it to be a continuous ordeal with a week or so between most things, that's why I'm having difficulty thinking of various enemies &amp; monsters to use without making it seem like monsters are a dime a dozen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T15:14:55-08:00","id":377560,"title":"","content":"Autch, yeah. If you want to go the &quot;Monster of the week&quot; route, you're gonna have to think of something.<br /> You could always have their first hunt be against some Horror, wishing to unleash its breathren/kinsmen?<br /> Like what if a dig for a new sub-way tunnel uncovers some ancient masonery, scribed with runes in long dead tongues with vague outlines of prison bars. While the government is debating what to do about it, the site is badly damage - though not entirely destroyed - by &quot;Teenage vandals&quot;, and all sorts of horrors creep out from this underground prison?<br /> Lucky for them, only the &quot;Teenage Vandal&quot; has the brains to realize that the prison is still intact enough to contain the rest of its brrod, but its preparing for another strike. And soon...<br /> Something like that might work. Then theres a very concret reason as to why theres so many monsters. You also have the possibillity of throwing in some political play, if the government decides to demolish the site anyway, and the Hunters need to stop that to prevent more horrors from comming loose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T10:21:56-08:00","id":378161,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you want it to be a &quot;one monster every week&quot; situation, you're going to have to come up with something to make it work. Krobeles' idea of some shit going down in the first chronicle/chapter that makes monsters pop up like crazy might work. Normally, your question would be somewhat academic, since hunter simply don't know about most supernaturals in their area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T11:25:22-08:00","id":378233,"title":"","content":"Think of each hunt in terms of 7 stages. Each stage moves as fast as the play group wants them. This will make sure &quot;Monsters of the week&quot; are more slowly paced and less likely to become a running joke.<br /> <br /> 1. Find a problem. This is the easy part, usually its something close to home that inspires the players to dig beneath surface explanations and uncover the supernatural.<br /> 2. Investigate the problem. Now that they have a problem and they're suspicious, they'll find out that the cause isn't human.<br /> 2 A. Reflect. Something inhuman, unnatural and not real, is totally real! How do your hunters handle this?<br /> 3. Find a suspect. So, the supernatural is totally real how do you go about finding who is, or more importantly who isn't, inhuman.<br /> 4. Surveillance. You have a suspect, but now you need to prove he's not human and figure out when to strike<br /> 4 A. Reflect. You're planning on maybe killing someone. Like seriously, killing or kidnapping another person because they might be something unnatural. How do you feel?<br /> 5. Plan. You've gathered information, you're sure that you're ok with going on the offensive, how are you gonna do it?<br /> 6. Action. You make your move and act. Maybe the hunters will be lucky enough to kill the thing.<br /> 7. Re-examine. Look back on what you did. If you killed it, what worked best, who did which jobs well. If it escapes, figure out how to do the job better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T14:35:55-08:00","id":378384,"title":"","content":"That kind of follows my first idea then, it was for the first monster/monsters the group kills leaves a hugh power vacuum, leading to lost of new monsters to come running. Also... any tips to do the whole are they/aren't they with monsters in human guise? I was hoping i needn't do that. I'd rather stay away from the theme of you might be killing an innocent til later when I want it to matter, I see no reason to constantly harass the players with possible evil actions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T17:39:44-08:00","id":378542,"title":"","content":"What is this &quot;evil&quot; you are talking about?<br /> <br /> More seriously, Hunter is about playing unhinged vigilantes; other than Promethean, it's probably the best group to play MurderHobos<sup>TM</sup> with. In other words, as long as you don't put any effort into making them feel bad about what they're doing, they'll happily hunt whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}